diff --git a/docs/UPGRADE.md b/docs/UPGRADE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..643a7ef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/UPGRADE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Rails and Ruby Upgrade Notes
+
+## Ruby 3.2 / Rails 6.1 release
+
+- Production remains on Rails 6.1.7.10; the Ruby runtime moves from 3.0 to 3.2.
+- `.ruby-version` is set to Ruby 3.2.9 and the Gemfile requires Ruby >= 3.2.0 and < 3.3.0.
+- `config.load_defaults 6.1` is enabled, and the shared application config also selects 7.0 defaults when booted by the Rails 7 bundle. Existing application settings remain explicit where they override framework defaults.
+- `Gemfile.next` is a Rails 7.0.8.7 bundle for testing and the following release. It uses the Ruby 3.2 dependency set and a Rails 7-compatible SQL Server adapter.
+
+## Session and mail-link compatibility
+
+- `belongs_to_required_by_default` remains false during this rollout so Rails 6.1-style association validation does not become an unintended upgrade break. The Rails 7 release must audit and migrate associations before removing this override.
+- The existing `secret_key_base` and `secret_token` are not changed, so signed session cookies and application verifiers keep their key material across rollbacks.
+- Rails 6.1 already uses SHA1 for signed-data key derivation. This release keeps that compatibility explicitly with `active_support.hash_digest_class`, `key_generator_hash_digest_class`, and `cookies_digest` set to SHA1.
+- The signed-cookie serializer is `:hybrid`. It continues to read existing Marshal-format cookies and writes the JSON format on migration.
+- Mail links generated with `Mailer.mail_link_token` continue to use the same verifier name, purpose, expiry, and SHA1 key derivation. Links sent before a Rails 7 rollout remain valid while this compatibility setting remains in place.
+- Nested session hashes for authentication registration and saved queries are normalized with indifferent access because `:hybrid` cookies may deserialize nested keys as strings.
+- Rails 7 test-fixture date formatting uses `to_formatted_s(:db)`, and the ActionView resolver patch accepts both the Rails 6.1 cached resolver API and the Rails 7 direct lookup API.
+
+## Rails 7 release work
+
+- Run the Rails 7 bundle with `BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.next bundle ...` and keep `config.load_defaults 7.0` in the next release.
+- The next release must retain the SHA1 key-digest and `:hybrid` cookie compatibility settings until existing cookies have migrated and every still-valid mail sent by Rails 6.1 has expired.
+- Run existing session/login and mail-link tests under both bundles. Remove the compatibility settings only after the rollback window is closed and the old signed payloads have aged out.
+- Add a Rails 7 lock refresh (`Gemfile.next.lock`) and resolve any remaining 7.0 framework deprecations before removing the temporary overrides.
